{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod","id":966376,"title":"First and Indigenous Peoples in CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T12:22:55-07:00","id":966376,"title":"First and Indigenous Peoples in CoD","content":"So by now we all know that the &quot;Magical Native American&quot; trope is played out to death, but how do you guys think tribes and bands can be used in CoD without playing to stereotypes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:38:04-07:00","id":966385,"title":"","content":"You treat them like human beings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:25:31-07:00","id":966410,"title":"","content":"People are people. But stereotypes <i>do</i> exist.<br /> <br /> You can either:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Ignore the stereotype. It informs nothing about the character. Where they match or oppose it is only incidental.</li> <li>Play against stereotype. Pick some or all elements and do the exact opposite. Show how ignorant and/or artificial the stereotype is.</li> <li>Justify the stereotype. Pick some elements and figure out <i>why</i> they might have led to a stereotype to begin with. This can be mixed with 2 in that some things were hasty generalizations, or due to misunderstandings.</li> </ol>Secondly, how prevalent is the stereotype, and how does the character react to it?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Ignores it, and treats attempts to fit them into the box as stupid.</li> <li>Deliberately acts counter to it in defiance or to prove how wrong it is.</li> <li>Embraces it as a cultural touchstone, or factual statement. (Widespread reactions of this nature may be why the stereotype persists)</li> <li>Uses it. Pretends to elements to fool people.</li> </ol>I'm probably missing some things. Big thing is: how big a role do you want the stereotype to play? If you don't care, then just eliminate or ignore it. But if it exists, figure out <i>why</i> and how accurate it might be.<br /> <br /> And always remember people will be people and deviate even from supported stereotypes (which are just commonalities, after all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-09-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:12:08-07:00","id":966457,"title":"","content":"A few things. First, remember that &quot;native&quot; and &quot;tribe&quot; are both considered racist terms when used to refer to communities in Africa. They are acceptable terms when used to refer to communities in North and South America. It's also more appropriate, regardless, to be more specific. &quot;The Creek,&quot; etc. In Europe, it's pretty much always more appropriate to say &quot;the Sami&quot; than to talk about tribes.<br /> <br /> I'm going extremely general, but I hope this is helpful. It also all depends on what time period you're running the game in, but I've never heard an Africanist claim it's acceptable to use &quot;native&quot; or &quot;tribe&quot; in reference to communities in Africa. Keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> Also, never ever ever ever use ~you're cursed because ancient indigenous burial site~.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:16:48-07:00","id":966698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966457#post966457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, never ever ever ever use ~you're cursed because ancient indigenous burial site~.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about when said burial sight is legitimately haunted by actual Ghosts, or if it doubled as containment for something else and was actually set up with a conditional curse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:02:55-07:00","id":966737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966698#post966698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about when said burial sight is legitimately haunted by actual Ghosts, or if it doubled as containment for something else and was actually set up with a conditional curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:38:50-07:00","id":966773,"title":"","content":"Is there any information anywhere about pre-contact aboriginal Vampires? I can't help but wonder just how Vampires would get by in a land where most people are nomads.<br /> <br /> Werewolf 2e briefly talked about aboriginal Werewolves in the Alice Springs writeup, which I liked.<br /> <br /> The only real thing I know that involves aboriginal stuff in Mage involves the Astral. I don't know if there's anything else.<br /> <br /> In my personal notes for my Chronicles of Darkness, I have it down that Extempores have historically been much more common in Australia than elsewhere. That's just a headcanon, but I like the thought of the most lonely of Prometheans walking the Pilgrimage in a land where everyone's on the move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 09-10-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:20:57-07:00","id":966810,"title":"","content":"Native Americans had static cities and towns, too. There's some mentioned in the Ancient Mysteries or Bloodlines books, and the Nosferatu clanbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:21:59-07:00","id":966889,"title":"","content":"True. Again, try to avoid generalizing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966698#post966698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about when said burial sight is legitimately haunted by actual Ghosts, or if it doubled as containment for something else and was actually set up with a conditional curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Flip the script: cursed/haunted imperialist colony burial site. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:23:43-07:00","id":966890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966889#post966889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flip the script: cursed/haunted imperialist colony burial site. \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>All for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:52:43-07:00","id":966909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966889#post966889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flip the script: cursed/haunted imperialist colony burial site. \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>Go one further. Cursed Norse burial site that the native Americans unwittingly built upon. A Norse burial site likely dates to around 1000 - 1010 AD, which is more than enough time for it's existence to be lost to the mists of history.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:01:52-07:00","id":966936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966909#post966909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go one further. Cursed Norse burial site that the native Americans unwittingly built upon. A Norse burial site likely dates to around 1000 - 1010 AD, which is more than enough time for it's existence to be lost to the mists of history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Norse burial site where? The failed Swedish colony is much much later than when you're talking about. I'm not sure what you're referencing, to be honest<br /> <br /> (Unless you're talking about alleged settlements in places like Rhode Island and MA. There is no legitimate reason to claim that Stone Tower, for example, was Norse.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:25:58-07:00","id":967008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966936#post966936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...Norse burial site where? The failed Swedish colony is much much later than when you're talking about. I'm not sure what you're referencing, to be honest<br /> <br /> (Unless you're talking about alleged settlements in places like Rhode Island and MA. There is no legitimate reason to claim that Stone Tower, for example, was Norse.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Anywhere between Newfoundland and Montreal. I rather scoff at the prospect of the latter, but having been in Iceland this summer, I can attest that some historians there argue that Vinland was that far into the interior. Northeast Canada seems pretty reasonable to me though. <br /> <br /> And of course, there is always the matter of those mysterious Irish Monks that were supposedly on Iceland before the Norse. They had to go somewhere. But I digress from our topic. <br /> <br /> One important note I'd say is if you are featuring First Nations, use their names for themselves in their language. It always gets my hackles up when someone refers to Kainai as &quot;The Blood Tribe&quot; since that name is a mistranslation. Even in cases where the translation is correct, such as Blackfoot for Siksika, decolonizing your language is easy to do and helps to show respect for the Nation's language, culture, and traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:46:46-07:00","id":967018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967008#post967008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anywhere between Newfoundland and Montreal. I rather scoff at the prospect of the latter, but having been in Iceland this summer, I can attest that some historians there argue that Vinland was that far into the interior. Northeast Canada seems pretty reasonable to me though.<br /> <br /> And of course, there is always the matter of those mysterious Irish Monks that were supposedly on Iceland before the Norse. They had to go somewhere. But I digress from our topic.<br /> <br /> One important note I'd say is if you are featuring First Nations, use their names for themselves in their language. It always gets my hackles up when someone refers to Kainai as &quot;The Blood Tribe&quot; since that name is a mistranslation. Even in cases where the translation is correct, such as Blackfoot for Siksika, decolonizing your language is easy to do and helps to show respect for the Nation's language, culture, and traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, for sure, Vinland. But I don't consider that a North American settlement as such. It's definitely something one could debate, that's completely legitimate.<br /> <br /> And I agree on the second point as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:15:17-07:00","id":967037,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about this recently. I'm running Mage in the Los Angeles setting and I'd like to incorporate the Dreamspeakers legacy as part of the chronicle since they're so tied to the Astral and they represent a very different idea of magic than Diamond orthodoxy, but I'm carefully considering exactly how I want to do it. From an OOC/game design perspective, the Dreamspeakers are kinda derived from a melange of Native American and Aboriginal ideas about magic and shamanism, but they're written as having spread to other people as well, especially fringe psychotherapists and Timothy Leary-esque psychonauts who interpret the Legacy in a slightly different way. I think that origin and split is a cool idea to run with, and I want to have some Dreamspeaker NPCs who are Native and happen to live in LA, and others who aren't linked to traditional shamanism at all. What I don't want to do is depict Native characters as somehow inherently magical and/or linked to this one specific style of practicing Awakened magic. One way of addressing that might be depicting other Sleeper/Sleepwalker characters who are indigenous, and/or making it clear that the Dreamspeakers are a living, vibrant legacy with their own shit going on apart from just channeling the idyllic past somehow.<br /> <br /> I think that's one of the big representation issues in CofD specifically because it's a setting about the supernatural hidden in the ordinary world, you don't want a situation where the only indigenous people who exist in your campaign are mysterious yet wise and helpful magical practitioners who only have agency relative to the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:41:23-07:00","id":967043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967037#post967037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking about this recently. I'm running Mage in the Los Angeles setting and I'd like to incorporate the Dreamspeakers legacy as part of the chronicle since they're so tied to the Astral and they represent a very different idea of magic than Diamond orthodoxy, but I'm carefully considering exactly how I want to do it. From an OOC/game design perspective, the Dreamspeakers are kinda derived from a melange of Native American and Aboriginal ideas about magic and shamanism, but they're written as having spread to other people as well, especially fringe psychotherapists and Timothy Leary-esque psychonauts who interpret the Legacy in a slightly different way. I think that origin and split is a cool idea to run with, and I want to have some Dreamspeaker NPCs who are Native and happen to live in LA, and others who aren't linked to traditional shamanism at all. What I don't want to do is depict Native characters as somehow inherently magical and/or linked to this one specific style of practicing Awakened magic. One way of addressing that might be depicting other Sleeper/Sleepwalker characters who are indigenous, and/or making it clear that the Dreamspeakers are a living, vibrant legacy with their own shit going on apart from just channeling the idyllic past somehow.<br /> <br /> I think that's one of the big representation issues in CofD specifically because it's a setting about the supernatural hidden in the ordinary world, you don't want a situation where the only indigenous people who exist in your campaign are mysterious yet wise and helpful magical practitioners who only have agency relative to the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the new importance given to Alexander's empire and the cultural confluence of Greek, Anatolian, Levantine, Egyptian, Persian, and Indian magic-users to the formation of the Diamond Orders in the backstory, you could say that the Dreamspeakers are the philosophical descendants of a Awakened cultural system that predated the Diamond, but faded away until only the Dreamspeakers remained. Maybe even say that this hypothetical other society pre-Colombian North American, and the Dreamspeakers were the equivalent of a Path that got subsumed into Diamond society. And if you don't want them to be all Native American, you could say that the Dreamspeakers allow anybody join in order to perpetuate the traditions of the pre-Colombian Awakened society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:58:42-07:00","id":967051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966457#post966457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few things. <b>First, remember that &quot;native&quot; and &quot;tribe&quot; are both considered racist terms when used to refer to communities in Africa. They are acceptable terms when used to refer to communities in North and South America.</b> It's also more appropriate, regardless, to be more specific. &quot;The Creek,&quot; etc. In Europe, it's pretty much always more appropriate to say &quot;the Sami&quot; than to talk about tribes.<br /> <br /> I'm going extremely general, but I hope this is helpful. It also all depends on what time period you're running the game in, but I've never heard an Africanist claim it's acceptable to use &quot;native&quot; or &quot;tribe&quot; in reference to communities in Africa. Keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> Also, never ever ever ever use ~you're cursed because ancient indigenous burial site~.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Why?! By who?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:06:21-07:00","id":967058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967051#post967051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Why?! By who?</div> </div> </div> </div>Africanists.<br /> <br /> I can't post history academic articles here, but a few accessible things come up from simple google searches:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://archive.learningforjustice.org/themes/custom/ts_ttol/img/lfj-share.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe\" target=\"_blank\"> The Trouble with Tribe </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> How a common word masks complex African realities. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.pambazuka.org/governance/what-word-tribe\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.pambazuka.org/governance/what-word-tribe</a><br /> <br /> Also, I'm not an Africanist myself, so I know very few personally, but you can email Elke Stockreiter at American University if you'd like more of an explanation.<br /> <br /> The gist is that &quot;tribe&quot; and &quot;native&quot;, when applied to Africa, have no coherent meaning, and were used by former colonial powers as negatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:08:51-07:00","id":967062,"title":"","content":"She talks about it some here, but you'll have to do further research on your own:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=AGqUBgAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA59&amp;lpg=PA59&amp;dq=elke+stockreiter+native&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=jEMTopS4Xc&amp;sig=gQxU_z3-TTahuDsHTEu3c-gnkmk&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiVy-rGnYbPAhWC0iYKHerjDSwQ6AEITDAI#v=onepage&amp;q=elke%20stockreiter%20native&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://books.google.com/books/publisher/content?id=AGqUBgAAQBAJ&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;img=1&amp;zoom=1&amp;edge=curl&amp;imgtk=AFLRE73Zam1eipELYqtLCWPGZtHsmxHndgPs0LCEHxWT3PVNXdZv-sRDoNsW_wQ354j5bRzu6PmAgcte8L8ej9cr8HrF8i3braVrUgRsFml7sFIIwi_a7G6YKA1Jm73iENTOmib_HYO9\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=AGqUBgAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA59&amp;lpg=PA59&amp;dq=elke+stockreiter+native&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=jEMTopS4Xc&amp;sig=gQxU_z3-TTahuDsHTEu3c-gnkmk&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiVy-rGnYbPAhWC0iYKHerjDSwQ6AEITDAI#v=onepage&amp;q=elke%20stockreiter%20native&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\"> Islamic Law, Gender and Social Change in Post-Abolition Zanzibar </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=AGqUBgAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA59&amp;lpg=PA59&amp;dq=elke+stockreiter+native&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=jEMTopS4Xc&amp;sig=gQxU_z3-TTahuDsHTEu3c-gnkmk&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiVy-rGnYbPAhWC0iYKHerjDSwQ6AEITDAI#v=onepage&amp;q=elke%20stockreiter%20native&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\"> https://books.google.com/books?id=AGqUBgAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA59&amp;lpg=PA59&amp;dq=elke+stockreiter+native&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=jEMTopS4Xc&amp;sig=gQxU_z3-TTahuDsHTEu3c-gnkmk&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiVy-rGnYbPAhWC0iYKHerjDSwQ6AEITDAI#v=onepage&amp;q=elke%20stockreiter%20native&amp;f=false </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> After the abolition of slavery in 1897, Islamic courts in Zanzibar (East Africa) became central institutions where former slaves negotiated socioeconomic participation. By using difficult-to-read Islamic court records in Arabic, Elke Stockreiter reassesses the workings of these courts as well as gender and social relations in Zanzibar Town during British colonial rule (1890-1963). She shows how Muslim judges maintained their autonomy within the sphere of family law and describes how they helped advance the rights of women, ex-slaves, and other marginalised groups. As was common in other parts of the Muslim world, women usually had to buy their divorce. Thus, Muslim judges played important roles as litigants negotiated moving up the social hierarchy, with ethnicisation increasingly influencing all actors. Drawing on these previously unexplored sources, this study investigates how Muslim judges both mediated and generated discourses of inclusion and exclusion based on social status rather than gender. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:22:07-07:00","id":967067,"title":"","content":"We are <i>really</i> getting to the point where people need to decide whether something said is offensive based off of the speakers intent rather than some inherent perceived wrongness based off of some past use of the word in some other time period or another because this is really starting to get ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:22:41-07:00","id":967068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967058#post967058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Africanists.<br /> <br /> I can't post history academic articles here, but a few accessible things come up from simple google searches:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://archive.learningforjustice.org/themes/custom/ts_ttol/img/lfj-share.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe\" target=\"_blank\"> The Trouble with Tribe </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.tolerance.org/magazine/number-19-spring-2001/feature/trouble-tribe </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> How a common word masks complex African realities. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.pambazuka.org/governance/what-word-tribe\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.pambazuka.org/governance/what-word-tribe</a><br /> <br /> Also, I'm not an Africanist myself, so I know very few personally, but you can email Elke Stockreiter at American University if you'd like more of an explanation.<br /> <br /> The gist is that &quot;tribe&quot; and &quot;native&quot;, when applied to Africa, have no coherent meaning, and were used by former colonial powers as negatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only ever heard African peoples referred to by name, so this is news to me. But if &quot;tribe&quot; is improper, what is the proper term for self-contained social unit of, say, Maasai? Village? Clan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:23:15-07:00","id":967071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967067#post967067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are <i>really</i> getting to the point where people need to decide whether something said is offensive based off of the speakers intent rather than some inherent perceived wrongness based off of some past use of the word in some other time period or another because this is really starting to get ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, but that's okay. We're clearly not talking about a past use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:24:34-07:00","id":967072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967062#post967062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She talks about it some here, but you'll have to do further research on your own:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=AGqUBgAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA59&amp;lpg=PA59&amp;dq=elke+stockreiter+native&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=jEMTopS4Xc&amp;sig=gQxU_z3-TTahuDsHTEu3c-gnkmk&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiVy-rGnYbPAhWC0iYKHerjDSwQ6AEITDAI#v=onepage&amp;q=elke%20stockreiter%20native&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.com/books?id=AG...native&amp;f=false</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In International Relations (IR) it's also frowned upon. While some still favor the term as a catch-all phrase for different ethnic groups, the usage becomes fuzzy super quickly. While it can be accurate to describe nomadic people's in Eurasia (though not always) it's often mis-used with respect to Africa. For example, people talk about the Hutus and the Tutsis refering to them as &quot;different tribes&quot; and that absolutely doesn't work. <br /> <br /> Further, there are empires that rivaled their European counterparts for large swaths of history, from Mali to various kingdoms in the African Great Lakes region (Where Rawanda is, btw) that you simply will not be able to accurately describe with a &quot;tribal&quot; framework at any point in history, much less today. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:28:27-07:00","id":967073,"title":"","content":"Clan MIGHT be right, but that's also a European construction.<br /> <br /> But also... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a>, we're literally talking about usage right now. Like. On this thread. like. RIGHT. NOW. NOW. NOT IN THE PAST. More importantly, the rule for whether or not someone can get offended doesn't work in /most/ cases. If I were to threaten Hayley with physical harm, she would have every right to take action to avoid that harm, whether or not it was a joke, or if I &quot;didn't mean it to be a threat&quot;. <br /> <br /> Intentions matter, but not as much as impact and consequences. In this case, referring to African society as tribal continues a misinformed idea of Africa as being backwards, uncivilized, and lesser. It matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:32:57-07:00","id":967078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967073#post967073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan MIGHT be right, but that's also a European construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't know enough about the current state of the field to comment about the appropriateness of &quot;clan&quot;, I just know that it was drilled into me by every Africanist I've ever met and every African history class I was ever required to through my degrees that &quot;tribe&quot; and &quot;native&quot; are racist when it comes to Africa. So I'll leave &quot;clan&quot; to you. Maybe send Stockreiter an email to ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:36:50-07:00","id":967084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967067#post967067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are <i>really</i> getting to the point where people need to decide whether something said is offensive based off of the speakers intent rather than some inherent perceived wrongness based off of some past use of the word in some other time period or another because this is really starting to get ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want to talk about right now, literally right now (and this just came back in 2011, when South Sudan became a country), the UN will not recognize new countries in Africa if they do not fall on former colonial European lines. Used in the last five years and still a UN policy <b>right now</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 09-10-2016, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:38:21-07:00","id":967087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967084#post967084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You want to talk about right now, literally right now (and this just came back in 2011, when South Sudan became a country), the UN will not recognize new countries in Africa if they do not fall on former colonial European lines. Used in the five years and still a UN policy <b>right now</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is entirely accurate. I had to read an account of the negotiations where the party for South Sudan had to find an older water rights contract so that part of their new country wasn't cut off from the other part. It was awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:06:26-07:00","id":967108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967084#post967084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You want to talk about right now, literally right now (and this just came back in 2011, when South Sudan became a country), the UN will not recognize new countries in Africa if they do not fall on former colonial European lines. Used in the last five years and still a UN policy <b>right now</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just due to stupid laws of large ruling bodies. I'm talking about person to person, using words for what they mean by actual definition rather than a government trying to abuse technicalities in old and/or poorly written terms of use as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:08:57-07:00","id":967110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967108#post967108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just due to stupid laws of large ruling bodies. I'm talking about person to person, using words for what they mean by actual definition rather than a government trying to abuse technicalities in old and/or poorly written terms of use as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actual definition.<br /> <br /> Written by whom? Sent down to the world with no context? Appearing in a book scrawled by...I don't even know whom, you tell me, whom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:10:00-07:00","id":967112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967108#post967108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just due to stupid laws of large ruling bodies. I'm talking about person to person, using words for what they mean by actual definition rather than a government trying to abuse technicalities in old and/or poorly written terms of use as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your position is that &quot;tribe&quot; and &quot;native&quot; are not racist terms when used to refer to members of ethnic groups in Africa, because those words have &quot;actual definitions&quot; that are not racist. Is that your claim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  Scare quotes, I admit it. 09-10-2016, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:18:48-07:00","id":967115,"title":"","content":"If you want to use the word tribe, you could use it in the context of Igbo Jews in Nigeria who claim they're the Lost Tribe of Israel.<br /> <br /> But to claim that the Igbo are a tribe shows a complete lack of awareness of the reality of ethnic relations in Africa. In real life right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:10:27-07:00","id":967139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967115#post967115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to use the word tribe, you could use it in the context of Igbo Jews in Nigeria who claim they're the Lost Tribe of Israel.<br /> <br /> But to claim that the Igbo are a tribe shows a complete lack of awareness of the reality of ethnic relations in Africa. In real life right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a question, does the technical definition of 'tribe' accurately describe the societal structure of groups of people in Africa? Are the people born there 'natives' of the continent by the technical definition of the word? Is it somehow inherently offensive to fit the descriptions of those words? Is it inherently offensive to <u><i><b>be</b></i></u> a 'native' to a certain region by the technical definition of the word or to be apart of the societal structure known as a 'tribe'? I would seriously think not. If anything it could be argued as being racist to say that being a native to any particular place is a bad thing, or to belong in a tribe is a bad thing. You could say that racists people do indeed say that being able to be classified under such terms are offensive, but that doesn't make the words themselves racists, it makes the people using them as such racist. They are words, and words have meaning, but the meanings of those words are usually not inherently offensive, and as such, the words themselves shouldn't be. I find it ridiculous that some people try to force them to be. <br /> <br /> Even assuming that the laws are trying to oppress a group of people using certain words, it isn't the words that are offensive, it is what is being done with them. The words are just words, sounds with meaning, usually unoffensive meaning. You can use unoffensive words in offensive ways and to do offensive things with but they aren't suddenly inherently offensive just because they can be misused. I would agree that both tribe and native <i>could</i> be offensive if used in a way to be so, as seems to be the case with whatever is/was happening wherever, but it should only apply in the context of it being used in a way that is meant to harm/offend, such as in the application of certain laws/rulings. <i>But</i>, when used with the intent to use the word for it's normal intended purpose, I see no reason for anyone to take offense, and find the act of doing so somewhat ridiculous. I respect peoples right to have an opinion on it and to be upset over whatever they choose to be upset on, but I still find it ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately it seems to be spreading, which is why I really wish people would move towards taking what is said by intentions and case of use rather than assuming that all uses of a certain word, even to certain people is somehow inherently offensive and 'racists' just because they choose to take offense from it, even when it is obvious that there is no offense meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:15:23-07:00","id":967141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967139#post967139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question, does the technical definition of 'tribe' accurately describe the societal structure of groups of people in Africa? Are the people born there 'natives' of the continent by the technical definition of the word? Is it somehow inherently offensive to fit the descriptions of those words? Is it inherently offensive to <u><i><b>be</b></i></u> a 'native' to a certain region by the technical definition of the word or to be apart of the societal structure known as a 'tribe'?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No.<br /> 2) Of the continent? That's not the definition you keep referencing, comrade.<br /> 3) Not offensive, as we've not talking about offense, and the question is based on a false premise, so I won't be attacking a strawman.<br /> 4) We're still not talking about offense =). However, tribe is a racist word that does not accurately describe any of the groups we are talking about. It would and does perpetuate harmful stereotypes about a group of people that still affects them to this day, as you seem to not understand.<br /> <br /> We don't live in a vacuum. You don't, I don't, none of us do. I don't believe you feel the need to claim that words exist outside of meaning and context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:18:36-07:00","id":967143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967139#post967139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately it seems to be spreading, which is why I really wish people would move towards taking what is said by intentions and case of use rather than assuming that all uses of a certain word, even to certain people is somehow inherently offensive and 'racists' just because they choose to take offense from it, even when it is obvious that there is no offense meant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;This rocket launcher I have is perfectly safe for children to play with. I don't PLAN or INTEND for them to launch it in the house.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;This grease fire I've started in the kitchen wasn't MEANT to burn out of control. You can't possibly be mad at me. Just because grease fires DO burn out of control doesn't mean that's how I MEANT for it to happen.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;I know I CALLED you a dirty ***** *****ing **** ***** ******, but I didn't mean to hurt your feelings or cause you harm. Don't take it that way, or you're the problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's racist for you to be affected in any way by unintentional racism.&quot; <br /> <br /> Frankly, I can't help but see my statements as logically identical to yours and I don't think the comparison looks favorable to you. <br /> <br /> Full disclosure, I flagged your comments. Maybe we should just let the mods take care of this at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:20:53-07:00","id":967144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967143#post967143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Full disclosure, I flagged your comments. Maybe we should just let the mods take care of this at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. I'm out too, for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:27:25-07:00","id":967146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967141#post967141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) No.<br /> 2) Of the continent? That's not the definition you keep referencing, comrade.<br /> 3) Not offensive, as we've not talking about offense, and the question is based on a false premise, so I won't be attacking a strawman.<br /> 4) We're still not talking about offense =). However, tribe is a racist word that does not accurately describe any of the groups we are talking about. It would and does perpetuate harmful stereotypes about a group of people that still affects them to this day, as you seem to not understand.<br /> <br /> We don't live in a vacuum. You don't, I don't, none of us do. I don't believe you feel the need to claim that words exist outside of meaning and context.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there are no groups in Africa belonging to a <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a social division in a traditional society consisting of families or communities linked by social, economic, religious, or blood ties, with a common culture and dialect, typically having a recognized leader? Alright, assuming that's true then it isn't the word to be applied. That said, the word <i>still</i> wouldn't be racist, it would just happen to be the wrong term for use, and anyone using it would simply be mistaken, not racist.<br /> <br /> Alright, using another one of the definitions, they are not a plant or animal (humans counting as animals)<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> of indigenous (meaning originating or occurring naturally in a particular place) origin or growth?<br /> <br /> Alright, you used to term racist. It isn't racist either. It doesn't inherently show a belief that one race is superior to or lesser than another race. There is nothing in the definition of either of those words that imply anything of the like.<br /> <br /> And I do not believe that words exist outside of meaning. They most certainly do, but saying that these words are automatically racist when used in the context of a certain place is not looking at the greater context of what it means and is being used for on a case by case basis. </span></span><br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:34:06-07:00","id":967153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967143#post967143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;This rocket launcher I have is perfectly safe for children to play with. I don't PLAN or INTEND for them to launch it in the house.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This grease fire I've started in the kitchen wasn't MEANT to burn out of control. You can't possibly be mad at me. Just because grease fires DO burn out of control doesn't mean that's how I MEANT for it to happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I know I CALLED you a dirty ***** *****ing **** ***** ******, but I didn't mean to hurt your feelings or cause you harm. Don't take it that way, or you're the problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's racist for you to be affected in any way by unintentional racism.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frankly, I can't help but see my statements as logically identical to yours and I don't think the comparison looks favorable to you.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, I flagged your comments. Maybe we should just let the mods take care of this at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those statements don't really mean much unless used in context. If there's no rocket launcher, or grease fire, I don't really see the problem. If there is, the problem isn't your words, it's that there is a rocket launcher or grease fire. <br /> <br /> As for calling someone whatever it is you're calling them, if you can name me a context in which those aren't being used directly in an offensive manner then color me impressed, and I guess no, it isn't a problem. Otherwise you are using it with the intent to be offensive, and as I mentioned, intent is what matters.<br /> <br /> And what are you flagging me for? Differing opinions? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:41:52-07:00","id":967156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967146#post967146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there are no groups in Africa belonging to a <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a social division in a traditional society consisting of families or communities linked by social, economic, religious, or blood ties, with a common culture and dialect, typically having a recognized leader? Alright, assuming that's true then it isn't the word to be applied. That said, the word <i>still</i> wouldn't be racist, it would just happen to be the wrong term for use, and anyone using it would simply be mistaken, not racist.<br /> <br /> Alright, using another one of the definitions, they are not a plant or animal (humans counting as animals)<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> of indigenous (meaning originating or occurring naturally in a particular place) origin or growth?<br /> <br /> Alright, you used to term racist. It isn't racist either. It doesn't inherently show a belief that one race is superior to or lesser than another race. There is nothing in the definition of either of those words that imply anything of the like.<br /> <br /> And I do not believe that words exist outside of meaning. They most certainly do, but saying that these words are automatically racist when used in the context of a certain place is not looking at the greater context of what it means and is being used for on a case by case basis. </span></span><br /> </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Truly last comment in response to you, and then I'm letting the mods handle it, because ObrimosMaintenance is right, this is no longer worth my time.<br /> <br /> You need to define your terms much more carefully, because no, that's not what a tribe is, and even if that were what a tribe is, that does not describe, for example, the Shona in Zimbabwe, nor the Hausa in Nigeria, nor x, y, z, I could go on to ethnic groups throughout Islamic Africa, East Africa, Central Africa, and the rest of the continent. It doesn't apply to white South Africans. It doesn't apply to Southern Africans in any of the countries in Southern Africa either. No. Unless you would call white people in Marathon, FL a &quot;tribe&quot;. Which you wouldn't. Because you understand the implications of the word, racist implications set by Europeans still upheld.<br /> <br /> Intent is completely and entirely irrelevant to whether or not you've caused harm. If I accidentally step on your foot and break your toe, I didn't MEAN to break your toe, but your toe is still broken, and it still really hurts. Instead of talking about what you *meant* to do, let's talk about what you actually did.<br /> <br /> Using the terms &quot;tribe&quot; or &quot;native&quot; to refer to people in Africa is racist. It has been explained to you from a history academia position and from an IR academia position. You can take it or leave it. I don't much care what you do. I'm bored, and I won't be wasting my time any longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:49:37-07:00","id":967160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967156#post967156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truly last comment in response to you, and then I'm letting the mods handle it, because ObrimosMaintenance is right, this is no longer worth my time.<br /> <br /> You need to define your terms much more carefully, because no, that's not what a tribe is, and even if that were what a tribe is, that does not describe, for example, the Shona in Zimbabwe, nor the Hausa in Nigeria, nor x, y, z, I could go on to ethnic groups throughout Islamic Africa, East Africa, Central Africa, and the rest of the continent. It doesn't apply to white South Africans. It doesn't apply to Southern Africans in any of the countries in Southern Africa either. No. Unless you would call white people in Marathon, FL a &quot;tribe&quot;. Which you wouldn't. Because you understand the implications of the word, racist implications set by Europeans still upheld.<br /> <br /> Intent is completely and entirely irrelevant to whether or not you've caused harm. If I accidentally step on your foot and break your toe, I didn't MEAN to break your toe, but your toe is still broken, and it still really hurts. Instead of talking about what you *meant* to do, let's talk about what you actually did.<br /> <br /> Using the terms &quot;tribe&quot; or &quot;native&quot; to refer to people in Africa is racist. It has been explained to you from a history academia position and from an IR academia position. You can take it or leave it. I don't much care what you do. I'm bored, and I won't be wasting my time any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>By current definition that is exactly what a tribe is. And I never said it applied to everyone in every ethnic group in Africa or anywhere else. Of course it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> And if you didn't mean it, no offense would be taken. It was an accident, and chances are it isn't going to do any real lasting harm so I'd get over it. I'm not going to have you arrested for assault and attempted murder and have you thrown in jail just for a little accident.<br /> <br /> You have explained your position and I have explained mine. I never really intended to try to change your outlook because it (usually) takes more than a few messages on the internet to change someones viewpoint and I have neither the time nor the inclination to attempt such tonight. I merely explained my outlook, which is one you clearly disagree with, and <i>that's fine</i>. That is your right. You don't <i>have</i> to agree with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:43:00-07:00","id":967185,"title":"","content":"Threads like this make me think a Sad Puppies or Gamer Gate situation is inevitable for us, too.<br /> <br /> As to the original thread topic - I agree with <b>Vent0</b>. People aren't stereotypes*, but stereotypes didn't arise out of nothing - they often reflect real social and cultural phenomena (usually problems). Don't embrace the stereotype - that's a waste of a character - but if the natural progress of a character's development requires that they &quot;go there&quot;, don't shy away from it. Everyone is flawed, after all, and forcing a character to be unnaturally perfect isn't good, either. <br /> <br /> Legacy-wise, most of the older Legacies are appropriate. The Fall makes it impossible to pinpoint an origin for any of the ancient Legacies, after all. The Dreamspeakers claim to be the <i>original</i> mages, older even than Atlantis, who first found the Isle of Dragons. Its canon that the Elemental Masteries are a worldwide phenomena, found among all the peoples of the world. And so on. With their origins lost, who can say what's &quot;authentic&quot; Native American magic, or African, or . . . .<br /> <br /> And its always fun to use the Fallen Pillar to smack pretentious mages in the face, when it turns out that that the &quot;street bum&quot; is actually the most powerful Thyrsus in a hundred mile radius<br /> <br /> The old World of Darkness has some good material, too. Vampires among the Aztecs, Greymere Glen is a &quot;haunted&quot; faerie stronghold accidentally created by fallen Vikings (and in North America, too) . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *although (in real life) I've known people who thought it was funny to play to the relevant stereotype, just to mess with a prejudiced individual","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:52:03-07:00","id":967205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967018#post967018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, for sure, Vinland. But I don't consider that a North American settlement as such. It's definitely something one could debate, that's completely legitimate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I was referring to Vinland. You don't need a successful settlement in order to create a burial ground.<br /> <br /> That said the WoD doesn't need to be historically accurate. Whatever Stone Tower is in the real world shouldn't stop it being created by Viking mages (or something) in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967156#post967156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to define your terms much more carefully, because no, that's not what a tribe is</div> </div> </div> </div>Most words have multiple definitions - an inevitable consequence of there being central authority curating the canonical definition of words.<br /> <br /> Ashenrogue's definition is taken from the Oxford Dictionary. It's as valid a definition of the word Tribe as any other definition you might find; and it's the one I use when I describe myself as a member of a Tribe. I can't remember where I first heard it, but someone suggested the answer to the eternal question of are Jews a religion or an ethnicity is that Jews a Tribe, and going by the Oxford dictionary definition I was persuaded. (Also I'm probably a member of one of the 12 Tribes of Israel. I have no idea which one though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-11-2016, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:02:17-07:00","id":967291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967205#post967205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ashenrogue's definition is taken from the Oxford Dictionary. It's as valid a definition of the word Tribe as any other definition you might find; and it's the one I use when I describe myself as a member of a Tribe. I can't remember where I first heard it, but someone suggested the answer to the eternal question of are Jews a religion or an ethnicity is that Jews a Tribe, and going by the Oxford dictionary definition I was persuaded. (Also I'm probably a member of one of the 12 Tribes of Israel. I have no idea which one though).</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're using a colonizer's definition. Today, right now.<br /> <br /> I'm letting the mods handle this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:16:21-07:00","id":967321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967291#post967291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're using a colonizer's definition. Today, right now.<br /> <br /> I'm letting the mods handle this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a completely valid definition of the word. And I'd guess that when most people use the word, they're using the &quot;colonizer definition&quot; if that's what you want to call it, which is isn't racist because it implies nothing that can be construed as possessing the qualities of racism. Now if you're using some other definition of the word, them it is up to the person listening to be able to tell the difference between which meaning of the word is being used at the time based on the context of the sentence it is being used in. Is the person clearly trying to be insulting and racist? If not, then chances are they're using the &quot;colonizer definition&quot; and aren't using whatever seemingly inherently racist definition you're using. Context matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:26:40-07:00","id":967326,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Alright, this conversation is not going anywhere. Everyone's personal opinions on the matter aside, intent is not the metric the mod team uses to judge whether or not a post is in violation of the rules, so all would do well to respect when people say &quot;these words are hurtful to me&quot;. Now let's get back to the actual topic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:35:16-07:00","id":967398,"title":"","content":"To refocus:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod#post966376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by now we all know that the &quot;Magical Native American&quot; trope is played out to death, but how do you guys think tribes and bands can be used in CoD without playing to stereotypes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, research. Read up on and understand your subject matter, ideally past and current. Let characters and situations flow from there.<br /> <br /> If you want to include stereotypes at all, justify elements (and lay out exactly what justifies them), invalidate elements (such as them being due to narrow context, misinformation, or being part of an agenda), or twist elements (such as &quot;people think X because of Y, but it is actually Z which only <i>seems</i> like Y, or Z itself leads to Y&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:04:51-07:00","id":967545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod#post966376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by now we all know that the &quot;Magical Native American&quot; trope is played out to death, but how do you guys think tribes and bands can be used in CoD without playing to stereotypes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd, if you want to avoid stereotypes, listen to Native Americans, read books written by them, ask questions from those who wish to answer them, and base you stories on theirs, not on those outsiders tell about them. It's become quite easy with Twitter and other social media.<br /> <br /> Also, ask yourself why you want to include them in your stories. If it's just as a prop, or plot device, it's perhaps not a good idea.<br /> It's unfortunately easy to include people from specific ethnicities in a story specifically because their stereotype fits a given narrative that way, so watch out for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:14:17-07:00","id":967702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966385#post966385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You treat them like human beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably without including any aspect of their culture, otherwise its problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:17:29-07:00","id":967704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=966457#post966457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few things. First, remember that &quot;native&quot; and &quot;tribe&quot; are both considered racist terms when used to refer to communities in Africa. They are acceptable terms when used to refer to communities in North and South America. It's also more appropriate, regardless, to be more specific. &quot;The Creek,&quot; etc. In Europe, it's pretty much always more appropriate to say &quot;the Sami&quot; than to talk about tribes.<br /> <br /> I'm going extremely general, but I hope this is helpful. It also all depends on what time period you're running the game in, but I've never heard an Africanist claim it's acceptable to use &quot;native&quot; or &quot;tribe&quot; in reference to communities in Africa. Keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> Also, never ever ever ever use ~you're cursed because ancient indigenous burial site~.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was a game designer and I had to deal with all of these limitations, I simply wouldn't bother including any ethnic groups but generic white people. If there is no offence intended by what someone includes in fiction, then the offence lies with the person taking offence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:28:29-07:00","id":967709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967704#post967704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was a game designer and I had to deal with all of these limitations, I simply wouldn't bother including any ethnic groups but generic white people. If there is no offence intended by what someone includes in fiction, then the offence lies with the person taking offence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to consider reading posts by mods before you respond to things, as this has been addressed, and the ruling is not in your favor.<br /> <br /> I'll let Char handle it. My boredness has been growing my blocklist lately, off to add you =).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:42:48-07:00","id":967714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967143#post967143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;This rocket launcher I have is perfectly safe for children to play with. I don't PLAN or INTEND for them to launch it in the house.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This grease fire I've started in the kitchen wasn't MEANT to burn out of control. You can't possibly be mad at me. Just because grease fires DO burn out of control doesn't mean that's how I MEANT for it to happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I know I CALLED you a dirty ***** *****ing **** ***** ******, but I didn't mean to hurt your feelings or cause you harm. Don't take it that way, or you're the problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's racist for you to be affected in any way by unintentional racism.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frankly, I can't help but see my statements as logically identical to yours and I don't think the comparison looks favorable to you.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, I flagged your comments. Maybe we should just let the mods take care of this at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let me get this straight, you don't like what he said, even though he was perfectly polite, and then you flagged his post. If this is the attitude of Onyx Path Forums, with this intellectual tyranny, then you don't want anyone around who don't share your opinions. Your basiclly sentecing yourselves to an echo chamber where everyone on the inside is good, and everyone on the outside is bad and wrong. This is a bad idea, for you, for those of us who don't agree with you, and for any intellectual advancment of civillization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:45:04-07:00","id":967716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod#post966376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by now we all know that the &quot;Magical Native American&quot; trope is played out to death, but how do you guys think tribes and bands can be used in CoD without playing to stereotypes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty easily.<br /> <br /> Everyone's a snowflake. Are you the same as every one else of your ethnic group? Are you and all of them stereotypes? No. Either is anyone else.<br /> <br /> Is a person magical? If so, make it because that person is magical, not because their 'people' are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-11-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:49:47-07:00","id":967719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967156#post967156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truly last comment in response to you, and then I'm letting the mods handle it, because ObrimosMaintenance is right, this is no longer worth my time.<br /> <br /> You need to define your terms much more carefully, because no, that's not what a tribe is, and even if that were what a tribe is, that does not describe, for example, the Shona in Zimbabwe, nor the Hausa in Nigeria, nor x, y, z, I could go on to ethnic groups throughout Islamic Africa, East Africa, Central Africa, and the rest of the continent. It doesn't apply to white South Africans. It doesn't apply to Southern Africans in any of the countries in Southern Africa either. No. Unless you would call white people in Marathon, FL a &quot;tribe&quot;. Which you wouldn't. Because you understand the implications of the word, racist implications set by Europeans still upheld.<br /> <br /> Intent is completely and entirely irrelevant to whether or not you've caused harm. If I accidentally step on your foot and break your toe, I didn't MEAN to break your toe, but your toe is still broken, and it still really hurts. Instead of talking about what you *meant* to do, let's talk about what you actually did.<br /> <br /> Using the terms &quot;tribe&quot; or &quot;native&quot; to refer to people in Africa is racist. It has been explained to you from a history academia position and from an IR academia position. You can take it or leave it. I don't much care what you do. I'm bored, and I won't be wasting my time any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a person is offended, they have complete control over how they react to offence. No one can cause anyone physical harm by saying something that offends them. Your feelings are entirely under your own control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:53:07-07:00","id":967723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967702#post967702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably without including any aspect of their culture, otherwise its problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This is how these people live&quot; and &quot;this is how these people are a magical, dangerous Other&quot; are vastly different concepts, and I think it's a goddamn shame you can't see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:58:52-07:00","id":967726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967723#post967723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;This is how these people live&quot; and &quot;this is how these people are a magical, dangerous Other&quot; are vastly different concepts, and I think it's a goddamn shame you can't see that.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much time, energy, and effort would I have to put in to avoid seperating what might be offensive to some, to what would be interesting to a reader? What is &quot;magical, dangerous, and other, is what makes a culture interesting, especially in horror, where you are looking for the dark side of a given topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:03:40-07:00","id":967729,"title":"","content":"you all know that it really doesn't matter if something offends someone- but what the forum rules say, right?<br /> <br /> As for whether something if may offensive to someone- do what I would do. Ask someone from that background (actually, it is better to ask a number of them, and listen to their reasons. That's more or less what OP does right now, if I'm not mistaken)<br /> <br /> EDIT- seriously, people take this argument to the philosophical, metaphysical level about definitions and words and subjective meaning, when the rule is pretty simple. If a dominant amount of people feel offended, the chances are it is offending. A European can't decide whether the word &quot;tribe&quot; if offending for an African because they have their own reasons for why that words offends them. Let's stop talk about philosophy and academy, and start to remember that there are people behind this, and this is their will and we should respect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-12-2016, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:06:49-07:00","id":967730,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Hey, I said <b>drop it.</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12094_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12094\" data-vbnamecard=\"12094\">K9ine</a>, I'm giving you a thread ban. Next time someone tries to bring this line of discussion up in this thread again, the thread is getting locked.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T03:24:53-07:00","id":967842,"title":"","content":"A related thing I've been pondering for a while is how you incorporate Native American culture and religion (I guess) which has been deliberately appropriated.<br /> <br /> Specifically, Boston Unveiled for Mage has a number of references to the native american inhabitants of the Boston area having their own magical traditions and ideas (though it doesn't really say very much), that the two major European cabals have basically appropriated to themselves. Plus, there have apparently been people living in the Boston area for at least seven thousand years which would be comparable in era to the Vinca in The Sundered World.<br /> <br /> There's lots and lots of material there but the book doesn't really address the details. Most obviously the local Mysterium would presumably incorporate these elements into their Mystery Cult; but I have no idea how that'd look in practice. Presumably I'd want to avoid making them look like that fraternal society that dressed up as 'native americans' that I can't remember the name of, but then again, maybe that'd hammer home that the Boston Mysterium essentially stole a lot of their stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:06:04-07:00","id":967879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/966376-first-and-indigenous-peoples-in-cod?p=967716#post967716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a person magical? If so, make it because that person is magical, not because their 'people' are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though with that said, there <i>are</i> ways to make a &quot;people&quot; magical.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They possess some bloodline-bound magical trait (Proximus Dynasty?). Since those don't seem to be <i>entirely</i> inclusive (not everyone displays the traits), perhaps some kind of population bottleneck happened that eliminated all &quot;non-magical&quot; members. Over time, they'd diversify enough that not everyone would display the traits again, but if &quot;first contact&quot; (when the Stereotype forms) was soon enough after, it might be accurate in that, at that time, everyone of the group <u>is</u> magical.</li> <li>Societal constraints are such that only &quot;magical&quot; members are suitable with meeting with &quot;outsiders&quot; (those out of group). In that case, if the only members the Stereotype-Creating-Group meet are magical, it would be understandable (if incorrect) to assume that they all are magical.</li> <li>Local phenomena lead to the expression of &quot;magical&quot; traits. Due to influence of Spirits, Ley-Line confluence, leaky Infrastructure, or whatever, it may be that anyone who dwells in the area gains &quot;magical&quot; properties. If the group has settled in the area, and only that area, for a given length of time, they may all <u>be</u> magical (though this is due to environmental factors, and not their actual ancestry).</li> </ol>The point is to examine and think about potential causes. Those will themselves suggest where exceptions will crop up, and how appropriate any stereotypes formed actually are.<br /> <br /> * Note: due to the above examples requiring more ST control/alteration than the typical &quot;secret history&quot; required by the CofD, they are better served by fictional groups you come up with yourself. Unless everyone is fine with you rewriting the history of some extant group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}